 1077 "selection" 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425053 1078 #edb/ref 17592186425013 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425053 1079 #uuid "94de2c24-0666-5987-a3e2-ff3510e0a531" 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425054 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425015 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425054 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425016 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425054 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425027 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425054 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425037 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425054 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425045 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425054 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425054 1077 "selection" 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425054 1078 #edb/ref 17592186425015 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425054 1079 #uuid "e2de97f4-e366-599b-83d2-129fe88a95e1" 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425055 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425050 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425055 1069 "q-34763" 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425055 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425055 1071 "If $D=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,$ then $\\text{rank}(D)=$" 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425055 1072 #uuid "06e82198-39dc-5c74-b637-e63de9108225" 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425055 1074 "To find the rank of $D,$ we first reduce it to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns (or alternatively, it has exactly $3$ non-zero rows).\n\nTherefore, $\\text{rank}(D)=3.$" 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425056 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425051 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425056 1069 "q-34805" 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425056 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425056 1071 "Let $A$ be a $7\\times 12$ matrix that has $6$ **pivot** columns. What is the rank of the matrix?" 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425056 1072 #uuid "6826463c-847d-5512-b760-3fbeb596f635" 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425056 1074 "We know that $\\text{rank}(A)$ is the number of pivot columns in $A.$ \n\nSince we are told that $A$ has $6$ pivot columns, we have \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)=6.\n$$" 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425057 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425052 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425057 1069 "q-35285" 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425057 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425057 1071 "If \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -6 & -9 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}]$, then $\\text{rank}(A)=$" 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425057 1072 #uuid "6e4ed9e5-eccc-52bc-8945-b31db9b251e2" 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425057 1074 "To find the rank of $A,$ we first reduce it to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -6 & -9 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $2$ pivot columns (or alternatively, it has exactly $2$ non-zero rows).\n\nTherefore, $\\text{rank}(A)=2.$" 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425058 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425049 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425058 1069 "q-79560" 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425058 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425058 1071 "Which of the following matrices has a rank of $3?$" 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425058 1072 #uuid "8c046845-0154-54e8-9266-c14fc31a0fbc" 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425058 1074 "First, notice that a matrix of rank $3$ must have at least $3$ columns and at least $3$ rows. \nSo, we disregard the following matrices:\n\n- $A$ since it has only $2$ rows.\n\n- $B$ since it has only $2$ rows (and only $2$ columns).\n\n- $E$ since it has only $2$ columns.\n\nAlso, the matrix must have $3$ pivot columns. As we can see, the matrix $C$ has exactly $3$ pivot columns, while the matrix $D$ has only $2$ pivot columns. So, $\\text{rank}(C)=3$ and $\\text{rank}(D)=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the matrix $C.$" 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425059 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425047 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425059 1069 "q-139966" 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425059 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425059 1071 "If \n$W=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -4 & 6 \\\\ -1 & -6 & 4 & -7\\end{aligned}]$, then $\\text{rank}(W)=$" 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425059 1072 #uuid "a35aea07-c94b-5a19-9d28-82b8ec3131d0" 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425059 1074 "To find the rank of $H,$ we first reduce it to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -4 & 6 \\\\ -1 & -6 & 4 & -7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 6 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns (or alternatively, it has exactly $3$ non-zero rows).\n\nTherefore, $\\text{rank}(W)=3.$" 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425060 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425054 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425060 1069 "q-79559" 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425060 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425060 1071 "Which of the following matrices has a rank of $5?$" 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425060 1072 #uuid "cf208166-634c-5dd4-a095-ee064f03b9e3" 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425060 1074 "First, notice that a matrix of rank $5$ must have at least $5$ columns and at least $5$ rows. \nSo, we disregard the following matrices:\n\n- $B$ since it has only $2$ rows.\n\n- $C$ since it has only $3$ columns.\n\n- $D$ since it has only $3$ rows (and only $3$ columns).\n\nAlso, the matrix must have $5$ pivot columns. As we can see, the matrix $A$ has exactly $5$ pivot columns, while the matrix $E$ has only $4$ pivot columns. So, $\\text{rank}(A)=5$ and $\\text{rank}(E)=4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the matrix $A.$" 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425061 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425048 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425061 1069 "q-79157" 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425061 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425061 1071 "Let $B$ be a $4\\times 5$ matrix that has $3$ **pivot** columns. What is the rank of the matrix?" 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425061 1072 #uuid "d99c604a-a10b-57d3-8148-d6702b5326c3" 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425061 1074 "We know that $\\text{rank}(B)$ is the number of pivot columns in $B.$ \n\nSince we are told that $B$ has $3$ pivot columns, we have \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(B)=3.\n$$" 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425062 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425053 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425062 1069 "q-79405" 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425062 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534544 17592186045417 true] [17592186425062 1071 "Let $A$ be